      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Week overview",
        "body": "¿Qué aprendiste ayer sobre esta misma materia?\n\nEscribe aquí:\n____________________\n____________________\n____________________\n\n## Repaso\n\nThis week we keep working on: Review Spanish indicative tenses.\n\nRead each part calmly and try the activity.\n\nExplain one idea with your own words.\n\nThis week we learn to narrate **when** in Spanish: **one-word** verb forms or **two words** with **haber** plus the participle.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "heading": "one word",
        "body": "Five **one-word** stations with *cantar*: **canto**, **cantaba**, **canté**, **cantaré**, **cantaría** — same root, different time.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points."
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "heading": "two words",
        "body": "Two-word times always look like **haber** + **-ado/-ido**: *he cantado*, *había comido*; only **haber** changes with I/you/he.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points."
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "heading": "choosing",
        "body": "Choose by asking three questions: Is the past closed? Does the result still matter? Is it background or habit?\n\nMira este ejemplo. Look at this example. Say one sentence about what you learned.\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points."
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "heading": "Synthesis",
        "body": "If you can build one clear example of each path, you hold the heart of this week’s Spanish times.\n\nMira este ejemplo. Compare \"Synthesis\" with something at home. How are they alike?\n\nPractice: Now it's your turn. Your turn. Say the key idea out loud. Draw one clear symbol or small scene about “Review Spanish indicative tenses”. Add one label from today's lesson.\n\nCommon mistake: Mixing up two different points.\n\n## Drawing for the image band\nDraw one clear symbol or small scene about “Review Spanish indicative tenses”. Add one label from today's lesson."
      }
    ],
